<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Camel warfare</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camel">Camel</a> warfare refers to the use of camels in combat, for transport of troops and supplies or as mounts. Camels' smell and appearance could unsettle horses, disrupting enemy cavalry. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a> deployed camels for this purpose, alongside war drums, as at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sagrajas">Battle of Sagrajas</a> in 1086.</p></div>
